WEBVTT

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.520
Look, the sky up above has begun to move.
Hora miageta sora ugokidashita yo

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.750
Your astonishment was so dazzling.
Odoroku kimi mabushikute

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.810
Should I forgive the lies you told me yesterday
Kinou tsuita uso mo yurusou kana

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.110
just because the morning light is so pretty?
Kesa no hikari kirei dakara

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:38.170
The sound of your laughter is always important to me
Kimi no warai goe itsu datte daiji da yo

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.820
because it gives me courage.
Yuuki kureru kara saa

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.680
It's not a lie.
Uso ja nai

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.460
It's a beauty really
It's a beauty really

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.610
Your voice whenever.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.110
It makes me have.
Your voice whenever.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:50.920
It makes me have.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.660
Even the silliest things sound dear,
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:57.980
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo
Even the silliest things sound dear,

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.540
if it's your voice I hear.
kimi no koe nara

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.810
You're sad whenever.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.480
It takes you back.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.840
My heart runneth over.
Hamidasu kokoro

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:16.040
Unable to control myself, I set off at a run.
Osaerarenakute hashiri dashita yo

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.050
I can forever.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:35.060
One, two, three, ta-dah!

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.240
Minamito Yui has gotten into Oumi Academy!

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.440
Congratulations, Yui-chan.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.360
Thank you, thank you.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.380
Why are you wearing your uniform
already? It's still March.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.380
She bought it on the last day of exams,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.400
because she was sure she got in.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.800
So, when do you plan on
moving into the dorms, Yui?

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.580
I can't have you invading my bed every time you come over.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.770
Well, there's something I've been
keeping secret from you.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.300
Oumi Academy is shutting down its dorms this year.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.400
Wait just a second!

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.890
Does that mean you'll be staying in my
room for three damn years?!

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.700
But I can't possibly live by myself.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.640
That's fine for now,
but what about summer?!

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.320
What will I do when you wake up in the
morning without any covers over you?!

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.940
What's wrong with her in the morning?

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.150
I can't tell them...

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:31.170
...that Yui has a habit of
undressing in her sleep.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.090
These fries are really
delicious, Mrs. Manaka.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.020
Oh, really?

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.910
Wait, didn't you...

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.210
Junpei, foot off the table!

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.940
Oh yeah, tomorrow's White Day.
Did you buy return gifts, Junpei?

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.260
You just tried to change the subject, didn't you?

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.420
Are you sure?

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.940
If you call yourself a man,

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.600
you should buy return gifts,
even for obligatory chocolates.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.660
I'll go with you and help you choose.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.670
Let's get going!

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.400
Huh?

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.640
If we don't leave now, the stores will close.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.650
Mr. and Mrs. Manaka, see you later!

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.040
A Level Up in Gratitude

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.080
I really don't like this kind of store.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.800
Hey, hey, Junpei!

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.550
I passed my exams, so buy me this.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.560
What are you, stupid?

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.070
You <i>said</i> "I'll help you choose~!"

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:27.810
So don't choose things for yourself!

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.090
But...

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.470
I'll just decide myself!

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.440
Erm... this and this.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.490
Eh? Why, why?

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.640
Why the different return gifts for obligatory chocolate?

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.000
Who do you like more,
Satsuki-chan or Toujou-san?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.270
Stop bugging me.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.540
The only difference
between these is 200 yen.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.970
The one with the bear is better from any perspective.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:48.700
I don't care.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:54.670
The store employees were staring at us because you were yelling.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:58.030
Only because you wouldn't tell me who you like more.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:02.470
Oh well. Either way, tomorrow will be a heartbreaking day for you.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.970
You just keep running that mouth!

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.640
I wish I'd given chocolates
to someone, too.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.620
Only because you want something in return.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.470
N-Nishino...

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.890
I-It's been a while.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.770
Is it just my imagination, or have you gotten taller?

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.120
I-I haven't seen you for
three months or so.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.590
That makes sense.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:32.990
See ya.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.430
That muffler!

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.350
Junpei, that person...
the chocolates...!

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:40.950
You know, the hand-made ones...

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.230
They were made by Nishino-san.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:45.140
Umm... you lost me.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:46.430
Satsuki made those.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.690
You're wrong!

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.080
I got lost on my way home from the entrance exams.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.610
Nishino-san helped me,
and that's when she told me.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:55.820
No way...

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:00.810
But, those chocolates <i>did</i> taste
as good as something store-bought.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.360
Nishino's about the only one who could pull that off.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:09.730
Back then, she said, "Thank you for eating the chocolates, Junpei-kun."

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.490
Junpei!

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.040
Why are you only telling me this <i>now?!</i>

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:21.750
Nishino!

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.300
T-Thanks for the chocolates. They were excellent.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.300
Thank you for realizing it.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.250
But, it would have been nice if you'd said that earlier.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.230
Y-Yeah, you got me there...

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.310
But you really are good at cooking, Nishino.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.640
Nishino really is cute.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.940
You didn't know until that girl told you, did you?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.620
Girl? What girl?

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:54.360
The girl who was
just with you? Yui-chan?

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.460
Oh yes, did she ever
get into Oumi Academy?

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.370
Yeah, pretty much.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.180
That means she'll be
an underclassman to you in April.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:08.460
I never thought I'd run into you at a time like this.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:11.480
Junpei-kun...

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.840
I've got an errand to run, so I should be going.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.730
W-Wait!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.560
Tomorrow's White Day, right?

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.760
I have to give you a return gift,
so what do you want?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.260
Not a thing.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:25.680
But...

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:28.990
I gave those chocolates to you out of gratitude.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:33.030
And I was okay with you not knowing they were from me.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:36.910
You see, during the time I went out with you...

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.520
... I think I "leveled up" quite a bit.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.450
After all, I even got accepted into Oumi Academy.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:45.680
Plus, I didn't just learn how to cook;

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:49.040
I also feel like learning to make all kinds of of things.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.630
But, when it comes to romance,

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.550
I don't think long-distance relationships work.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.580
To Nishino, my existence is...

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:02.270
Something that's already
part of the past.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.470
Junpei-kun, car!

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.110
You dummy!

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:11.020
If you keep spacing out like that, you're really going to die.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.810
S-Sorry.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:21.560
Even when we were dating, we were never this close.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.340
Just kidding! Sorry I said something weird.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.590
Well, I really do have to go.
Bye-bye, Junpei-kun.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:29.540
Nishi--!

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.510
I'm an idiot...

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:37.410
There's no way Nishino
would come back to me...

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.110
Junpei, what's wrong?

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:42.590
Here, you forgot this.

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:48.220
Yui, I'll give all of that to you.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:52.020
Eh? But, Junpei...
Wait a second, Junpei!

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.230
I'm not worthy.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:58.200
After parting ways with Nishino...

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.420
I haven't...

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.040
I haven't changed at all!

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.110
Junpei!

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.700
Today's White Day, isn't it?

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.620
You didn't forget
your presents, did you?

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:13.260
I mean, there's no guarantee you'll get any chocolates next year.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:15.790
I get it already.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.800
I wonder what I'll get today.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.150
I'm fine with anything <i>he</i> gives me.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.540
What is it, Manaka-kun?

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.220
Well, you see...

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:33.570
Here. Today's White Day, right?

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.880
I ran out of time, so I had to get it at a convenience store.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.690
Sorry.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:45.110
It's my first time doing something like this, so it's kind of embarrassing.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.700
This is also... my first time.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:56.420
S-Sorry. I know this
is White Day and all,

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.930
but I wasn't expecting a return gift...

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:04.940
This makes me so happy!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:08.480
So what is it? Isn't this a nice heart sticker?

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.870
I wouldn't know.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.600
I bought it at a convenience store,
so I didn't notice the sticker.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:17.240
Aw, come on! You can be honest with me, my darling~!

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:23.490
Oh, so you bought something
even nicer for Toujou-san.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.240
Hers is the same.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.210
I gave Toujou the same thing.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.830
Sorry. To tell you the truth,
that's what I was worried about.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:37.090
I thought that my chocolate sucked for sure.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:39.210
Yeah, about those chocolates...

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.750
Satsuki, where around my house
did you leave those chocolates?

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.200
What are you saying?

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:47.770
Didn't I leave them at the garbage can by the vending machine near your house?

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:52.390
Actually, they were pretty much defective goods.

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:55.800
You should've assumed that someone wanted to trash them.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.610
Still, I'm really impressed that you found them.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.440
Uhh... <i>yeah.</i>

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:03.690
You could say that the garbage
can was calling out to me.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:07.080
That's amazing! You might have psychic powers, Manaka!

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:10.070
But I'm glad they reached you safely.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.120
I've regretted trashing them ever since that day.

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:18.920
And, I'm happy you said they tasted good. Even if you lied.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.840
I-I wasn't lying.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:22.940
I'm sorry.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:24.980
I <i>was</i> lying.

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.510
There's no way they'd be here.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.980
It's been a month since Valentine's Day.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.230
...someone wanted to trash them.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:39.360
No matter how crappy they were,

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:43.370
I wish I could've eaten Satsuki's chocolates.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.760
But, no matter what I try to imagine,

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:50.410
the taste of Nishino's chocolates keeps coming back to me.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:55.380
I guess I haven't grinded enough to hear that "level-up fanfare."

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:27.170
Manaka-kun.

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:30.250
Today's date was really fun. Thank you.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.060
I had lots of fun too.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.940
Really? That's great.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:40.040
Would you please give me a memory of this fun day, Manaka-kun?

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.330
T-Toujou...

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.940
Junpei-kun.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.520
Manaka, me too.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.040
Manaka-kun...

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:52.780
Junpei-kun...

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:54.170
Manaka-kun...
Junpei-kun...

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:57.030
Junpei, wake up!

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:01.820
Didn't <i>you</i> ask me to wake you up early today?

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:06.070
Weren't you meeting up with Komiyama-kun today?

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.040
Oh, man, look at the time!

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.920
I-I'll be late!

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:19.050
You've been up late watching DVDs every night during spring break,

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.880
and now you can't wake up early.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.500
Shut up!

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.230
I'm gonna be late!

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.370
What a weirdo.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:28.130
He's just going to a movie with Komiyama-kun..

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:33.140
Beating Heart * First Date!?

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.440
I've kept it a secret from Yui, but...

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.560
Today's the day I promised to go to a movie with Toujou.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:43.300
My first date with Toujou,
and I overslept!

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:49.540
S-Sorry.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:50.910
I'm late.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.910
I just got here, too.

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:55.880
I-I see.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.150
What a relief.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.600
Are you okay?

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:02.200
Yeah, I'm completely fine.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:05.520
I hope we can make it to the movie on time.

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:08.590
We can. There's plenty of time before the next showing.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:11.090
Aha! Two students detected!

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.810
K-Kurokawa-sensei!
K-Kurokawa-sensei!

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.310
What are you two doing right now?!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.330
"W-What"?

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:21.630
We weren't really doing
anything wrong.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.070
Right, Toujou?

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.570
Y-Yes.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:28.320
Well, if you weren't doing anything, then...

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.580
Limited Time Offer
1 Pack Toilet Paper 50 Yen
Limit 1 per Customer

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.670
You have but one mission:

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.320
To exploit the "time sale"
at this drug store,

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:39.760
stand in line for one hour and purchase specially-priced toilet paper.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.590
So, when does this time sale start?

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:44.810
One hour from now.

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:48.170
What?! We have to stand in line for an hour?!

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.940
That's common sense, you fool!

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:53.380
Well, we'd really love to help, but--

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:55.600
All right, that's the spirit!

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.650
That's what makes you my students! Now, let's go!

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:03.270
Ah, I'm glad I got three of them.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:08.140
J-Just to buy 12-roll
toilet paper packs...

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:10.490
We stood in line for one hour.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:11.980
What's the big deal?

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:14.460
Next semester,
I'll up your grades a little.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.640
But we won't be in your class much longer.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.540
Don't sweat the small stuff.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.230
Manaka-kun, the movie...

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:22.000
Excuse us!
Excuse us!

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.040
Right, I'll be asking for help again!

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:33.150
Somehow, we made it in time.

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:34.050
Yeah.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:41.690
It sure is great...

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.400
...to have the same interests.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.800
I don't need to be too guarded.

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:49.680
We laugh at the same parts.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.150
We get excited at the same parts.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:56.370
And...

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.250
We cry at the same parts.

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:04.870
It was a good story, wasn't it?

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:06.020
Yeah.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:08.710
It was a good movie and I was next to Toujou.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.240
This is bliss...

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:13.470
What the heck was <i>that?</i>

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.180
I was expecting
to be floored, not bored.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:19.180
Who <i>is</i> this girl?

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:22.180
The main character was too wimpy.

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:24.460
He was powerless,
but he charged in anyway.

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:27.050
Why would anyone risk their life for someone like that?

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.320
It's far from explained.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.560
And then, his comrades
get defeated one after another.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:34.600
It's so sad I can't even cry.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:38.830
The CG was mediocre, too.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:39.750
Hey!

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:41.040
What?

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.150
Manaka-kun--

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:43.900
Aren't you saying a bit too much?

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.840
What, wasn't that all true?

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:50.380
Don't you know how much work
the staff put into this film?!

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.450
Movies live by their content.

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:55.310
And that content's ability to impress the viewers.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:58.710
The production year, the budgets...
they're all just numbers.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:02.890
B-But still, the movie had plenty of good points.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:06.590
Like what? Tell me, I'm all ears.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.900
L-Like how each of his comrades was unique.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:11.910
Really?

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:15.160
I couldn't even tell who was who.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:17.870
The fight scenes and the dungeons were amazing too!

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.510
So what?

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:23.830
If we don't see the special powers of the "special" sword, the story doesn't add up.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.140
I thought so, too.

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:27.690
So that's it...

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:30.820
The portrayal of the sword's powers <i>was</i> pretty vague.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.880
Yet they were forbidden to use it.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:38.730
See? This movie just wasn't impressive enough to me.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.540
Yeah, I guess not.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:42.760
That's not it!

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:47.390
You're just being critical.
Why not just watch it casually?

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:53.780
So, I guess you follow the "if you can't win by reason, go for volume" philosophy.

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:56.720
Forget her. Let's go, Toujou.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.020
Sorry for pointlessly wasting your time.

00:16:59.020 --> 00:16:59.980
It's okay.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:01.100
What?

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:04.210
You're retreating because you're with your girlfriend?

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:06.940
I suppose you just went to the movies

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:10.300
because you wanted to hold hands in the dark ambiance of the theater.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.040
It's disgusting, to be honest.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:15.770
So humiliating...

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:18.080
Humiliating, humiliating, humiliating!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.510
I'm so humiliated I forgot to buy a pamphlet.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:22.000
Manaka-kun.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.470
Are you okay?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.400
Why wouldn't I be?

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:29.090
I'm fine. There are lots of conceited girls like her.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:31.430
But...

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:33.770
I can't counter that girl's words.

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:35.900
I did enjoy the movie,

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:39.450
but she successfully pinpointed everything I had doubts about.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:40.990
Manaka-kun.

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:43.410
Aren't you thirsty?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.170
Why don't we go get
something to drink?

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:47.980
Y-Yeah.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.710
That's right.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.300
The movie was secondary.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:52.800
Wasn't my main goal today to be alone with Toujou?
The movie was secondary.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.220
Wasn't my main goal today to be alone with Toujou?

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:58.490
Hmm, where should we go?

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:00.610
Oh, wherever...

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.790
Any place you like is fine.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.760
Will you please choose, Manaka-kun?

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.020
Erm, then...

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.260
Welcome! Good evening.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:14.300
Of all places, I choose a burger joint?!

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:16.740
I should've picked
something higher-class.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.100
That's right.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:24.790
We could do some karaoke after this.
It's a standard date thing.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:28.320
Hey, would you like to go do some karaoke after this?

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:32.330
K-Karaoke...

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:37.800
Sorry, I'm really bad at karaoke.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:40.930
I get really nervous when I sing in front of people.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.940
Please, anything but that!

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:45.270
I understand. It's okay, it's okay.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.770
Not good. Another topic, another topic.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:53.200
Oh yeah, did you see the comedian championships on TV yesterday?

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.050
They were pretty funny.

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:57.480
I'm sorry.

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:00.320
I was reading a book all day yesterday.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.320
A-A book?

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.420
Yeah.

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:08.310
I-I haven't sat down and read a book in ages.

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:13.320
Another failure.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:14.850
What should I do?

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:16.500
I can't find anything to talk about.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:20.510
Do we really have so few common interests?

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:25.270
I might be able to burn some time talking about Toujou's novel.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:27.510
But we can't talk
about that all the time.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:29.920
What a waste of a date...

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:33.380
I sure am useless.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:34.550
Manaka-kun.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:37.890
That movie was interesting, wasn't it?

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:41.150
That person said some
harsh things back there.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:43.320
There was definitely room for improvement.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.770
But, I thought it was a good movie.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:49.580
After all, I was moved to tears.

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:52.370
What's important is
your feelings, right?

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:55.580
You shouldn't let others' opinions twist them, right?

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:57.120
Toujou!

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:59.780
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:02.710
I'm glad. I was really moved, too.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:06.600
If you also said it was boring,
I wouldn't know how to respond.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.300
Like in the last scene!

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.540
The protagonist was done well in that scene.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:13.100
Like, "I am victorious!"

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:18.120
Yeah! The first war scene really moved me, too.

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:19.520
It really was great.

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.800
Yeah, it was truly amazing.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:24.240
You can't pull off suspense like that so easily.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.890
It's gotten a bit late.

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:30.410
We went on and on about the movie.

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:34.520
What's wrong?

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:38.520
Actually, there's one last place I want to go.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:40.150
Fine, but where?

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.380
A bookstore.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:42.730
It's for...

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:45.910
What book did you read yesterday?

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.390
I want to read it too.

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:53.320
You don't need to buy it.
I'll lend it to you.

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:56.270
Thanks, but I want a copy for myself.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:59.850
But... it's a hardcover book, so it'll be quite expensive.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:00.840
Yeah.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:02.860
I'll be sure to read it.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:04.100
Okay.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:06.580
Huh?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:07.640
Look out!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:14.310
I'm sorry!

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:19.870
I'm sorry, Manaka-kun.
I'm sorry, Manaka-kun!

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:22.180
This soft sensation...

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:23.880
...is true bliss...

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:26.400
Huh?

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.930
I think I saw somebody
take a bad spill.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:31.600
Was it our fault?
If so, I'm speeding up!

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.000
How was the movie, Misuzu?

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.420
It was terrible.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:37.500
That's what you always say.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:39.090
It's just...

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:41.590
Why not just watch it casually?

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:46.170
I met an intriguing guy there.

